  "answer": "On the fixture estate that reproduces this program's measured trap, enablement is governed by enabledPlugins in ~/.claude/settings.json. The captured `claude plugin list` matches that map (harness@lab enabled, agentbridge@lab disabled, metaswarm@lab enabled) and contradicts both the root and per-project enabledPlugins maps in ~/.claude.json, which invert harness/agentbridge and invent root-ghost@lab. That is the right-key-wrong-file failure; the disagreement is a scope-mismatch finding, not a value to normalise. Mounted marketplace `lab` ships four plugins; harness@lab and metaswarm@lab contribute commands/workflows and are runtime-enabled; agentbridge@lab contributes a command file but is runtime-disabled; docs-only@lab is marketplace-only and contributes neither. On this Linux worktree live ~/.claude/settings.json, ~/.claude.json, installed plugin trees, the F-plugin registry, and the `claude` binary are all absent, so live settlement is UNVERIFIED. Catalog F-plugin n=21 cannot be joined without 08-WORKFLOW-CANDIDATE-REGISTRY.json.",
